# Composite figures

A bare `::: figure` opener is one figure of ordered panels (PART 9 4c).

::: figure
![Left panel](left.png)
^ (a) The left panel

![Right panel](right.png)
^ (b) The right panel
:::
^ Figure #: The two panels, side by side.

An opener carrying a quoted title is a generic container, not a group.

::: figure "A titled figure div"
Ordinary container content.
:::

So is one carrying a label.

::: figure [gallery]
Ordinary container content.
:::

Groups do not nest, so the inner opener below is a generic container.

::: figure
:::: figure
![Inner](inner.png)
::::
:::
^ Figure #: Only the outer opener is the group.

The same holds through one intervening container.

::: figure
:::: note
::::: figure
![Nested through a note](note.png)
:::::
::::
:::

Through a quote.

::: figure
> Quoted context.
>
> :::: figure
> ![Nested through a quote](quote.png)
> ::::
:::

And through a list item.

::: figure
- A panel with a caption below it.

  :::: figure
  ![Nested through a list item](item.png)
  ::::
:::

A group nested inside a container of another kind is still a group.

::: note
:::: figure
![Panel](panel.png)
::::
:::

The separator is a space run and never a tab, so the next line is a paragraph:

:::	figure
